## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] With no TLS variables, graph-manager starts on plain HTTP exactly as before; the startup line is `graph-manager listening on http://<host>:<port>` and the login cookie has no `Secure` flag (existing tests in `main.test.ts` and `auth.test.ts` pass unchanged).
- [ ] With `GM_TLS_CERT` and `GM_TLS_KEY` (or `--tls-cert`/`--tls-key`), `curl -k https://127.0.0.1:<port>/healthz` returns `{"ok":true}`, the startup line and returned `url` start with `https://`, and the login cookie is `Secure`.
- [ ] Only one of the two set: `loadConfig` throws `ConfigError("set both GM_TLS_CERT and GM_TLS_KEY, or neither")`; `graph-execution manager` exits 2 with that message.
- [ ] An unreadable file: startup fails (exit 1) with `cannot read TLS certificate <path>: <reason>` or `cannot read TLS key <path>: <reason>`.
- [ ] `GM_TRUST_PROXY` `1`/`true`/`yes` (any case) → `trustProxy: true`; unset/`0`/other → false.
- [ ] With `trustProxy` on and `X-Forwarded-Proto: https`, login sets `Secure` and logout clears with `Secure`; without the header, or with `trustProxy` off, no `Secure`.
- [ ] With `trustProxy` on, two clients with different `X-Forwarded-For` get separate failed-login buckets; with it off they share one.
- [ ] With TLS on, the terminals' `GM_INTERNAL_URL` is a plain `http://127.0.0.1:<other port>` listener that serves `/api/internal/*` only (404 for anything else), closed with the app; the URL printed after `graph-execution --sandbox` is the `https://` page (or `GM_PUBLIC_URL`).
- [ ] READMEs: the HTTPS setup section with the Tailscale, own-certificate (incl. Docker `/certs` mount) and Caddy recipes, the Install on a phone paragraph, the new variables in the configuration table, the new flags in the flags tables.
- [ ] Tests pass: `npm run typecheck && npm run lint && npm test`.

